<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chapultepec Peace Accords</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1992">1992</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvadoran-civil-war">Salvadoran Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chapultepec Peace Accords were signed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chapultepec-castle">Chapultepec Castle</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a> on 16 January 1992 by the government of El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/farabundo-marti-national-liberation-front">FMLN</a>, after negotiations under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> mediation. They ended the twelve-year Salvadoran civil war, reduced and reformed the army, abolished the old security forces, created a National Civil Police and turned the FMLN into a legal party.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chapultepec-peace-accords.jpg" alt="Chapultepec Peace Accords" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Presidencia El Salvador from San Salvador, El Salvador, América Central · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:XXIV_Conmemoraci%C3%B3n_de_los_Acuerdos_de_Paz._(24312587612).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
